# Normain — Leyton follow-up answers

Period assessed: Jul 2025 – Apr 2026. Drafted 2026-05-08.

## 1. Timeline and expected progression

- **Q3 2025** — RAG product in production; structured weekly evaluation against expected outputs shows quality is insufficient.
- **Oct–Nov 2025** — Decision to abandon RAG.
- **Dec 2025** — Agentic architecture becomes feasible (LLM tool-use maturity + internal experiments).
- **Dec 2025 – 10 Feb 2026** — Full rebuild: 9-tool agentic loop, virtual filesystem (content-addressable, symlinked, ripgrep-backed), cell-by-cell generation, new UI. Launched 10 Feb.
- **Feb 2026 – now** — Post-launch hardening at ~50–220 PRs/month. Active Linear projects: Stability & Quality, Improved source references, Run comparison, Document framework 1.x.
- **Next 6–12 months** — Trust/verification UX, PDF-page-accurate citations, audit-volume scale (100+ docs), reliable subdomain crawling, closed-loop eval harness, continued tool-set expansion. No feature freeze planned.

**Confidence: High.** Phases, dates and active workstreams are directly verifiable from Drive, git log and Linear. Forward ordering may shift with external pressure.

## 2. Uncertainties — evolving and unresolved

**Resolved**
- Agentic loop > RAG for structured knowledge work.
- Virtual filesystem (CAS + symlinks + ripgrep) usable while reorganising mid-indexing.
- Cell-by-cell generation cost-tractable in production.

**Reduced, not closed**
- Trust/verifiability UX — narrative reasoning and review mode shipped; raw tool-call trace still considered insufficient for non-technical reviewers.
- API-throughput stability under load (recurring fixes, not one-shot).

**Still open**
- PDF page-level citation accuracy across multi-column / reflowed / OCR'd inputs — dominant trust blocker.
- Subdomain web crawling (JS rendering, auth, dedup) — generic solution unsolved.
- Speed and scale at audit volumes (100+ docs concurrent).
- Closed-loop eval harness — no canonical metric for agentic structured extraction; metric design is itself a research problem.
- Validation mode integration into the main edit flow.
- Tool-set scope — every new dataset surfaces tool gaps.

**Confidence: High.** Categories trace directly to codebase and Leyton checklist.

## 3. Where experimental effort sits today

Work where the right approach is not known in advance and is iterated against real-world data:

| Area | Share | Why R&D |
|---|---|---|
| Trust UX + source-reference accuracy | ~40% | No published solution gives audit-grade citations from agentic extraction over arbitrary inputs. |
| Agent loop quality + tool design | ~25% | New datasets keep surfacing new failure modes; tool-set evolves empirically. |
| Speed/scale at audit volumes | ~15% | Concurrency, batching, model routing, queue stability — tuned per use case. |
| Web ingestion at scale | ~10% | Subdomain crawling, JS rendering, auth — no off-the-shelf solution. |
| Eval/regression infrastructure | ~10% | Metric for agentic structured extraction is a research problem. |

Excluded as non-R&D: routine UI polish, Vanta dep bumps, Azure infra, ISO/SOC compliance.

**Confidence: High thematic, medium percentages** — categories from recent commits and Linear; percentages are estimates, not tracked hours.

